# Story report

1. What the runs prove

Each claim below is checked over the flushed files; the verdict table (section 7) says whether it held.
An assertion checks one component's own numbers; an oracle check compares the proxy's numbers with an
independent record (the simulated clients, the fake Postgres or the load tool).

The report's structural checks:
- DuckDB: DuckDB is installed and is the pinned family 1.5.x (it reads the files)
- arguments: every argument is an existing directory
- runs: at least one run directory was found
- finished: every run directory has run.csv (the run finished)
- files: every run directory has metrics.csv and histograms.csv
- schema header: every file starts with the schema version 1 header
- schema guard: the complete runs pass test/analysis/guard.sql: schema version 1 in every row, no empty required field, one run.csv row and a distinct run id per directory, metric rows in every run

